# Architecture map (read first)

`DebuggerApp` (`cmd/gdbforge`) = **system-context orchestrator**. It owns and wires `GDBClient`, models, MCP/AI, and widgets. It is not “only” an MVC controller — it **hosts** GUI controller methods.

## Roles

| Piece | Role |
|-------|------|
| `DebuggerApp` | Orchestrator / system context |
| `cmd/gdbforge/*.go` methods | GUI controller (intents → model → Send / SetItems) |
| `internal/mcp` (`GdbMcpService`) | Peer controller (AI) on the same session |
| `internal/gdb` (`GDBClient`, `SendCmd`) | Shared session / pipe — not a controller |
| `internal/gdbforge/models` | Shared MVC data (`BreakpointList`, …) |
| `internal/gdbforge/domain` | `DebugDomain` surface for AI / future Lua |
| `internal/gdbforge/widgets`, `internal/termui` | Views only (paint + callbacks) |

## One shared resource, two controllers

`GDBClient` is owned by `DebuggerApp`. GUI and AI both use it. Widgets never own the session.

## Where to edit (common)

| Task | Look here first |
|------|-----------------|
| Set/clear BP (Space) | `widgets/code_widget.go` → `cmd/gdbforge/breakpoints.go` → `models/breakpoints.go` |
| BP list e/d | `widgets/breakpoint_widget.go` → `breakpoints.go` → model |
| GDB console submit/paint | `gdb_console.go` + `widgets/gdb_widget.go` |
| Threads / callstack | `debug_info.go` / `stopped.go` + widgets |
| `:b` completions | `buffers.go` (`bufferCompletions`, `bufferListed`) |
| AI / MCP tools | `internal/mcp/tools.go` + `cmd/gdbforge/debug_domain.go` implements `gdbforge/domain` |
| MVC docs | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` § MVC |

## Do not

- Put GDB `Send` / session ownership in widgets
- Duplicate breakpoint truth outside `models.BreakpointList`
- Treat `gdb.SendCmd` as the MVC controller (it is a transport helper)
